# Line-ending policy.
#
# Every text file is stored with LF in the index and checked out with LF, on every
# platform. Without this file the result depends on each developer's local
# `core.autocrlf`, which means the repo's correctness rests on machine configuration
# that is not part of the repo. This makes it repo state instead.
#
# It matters here beyond tidiness:
#   - scripts/deploy-escrow.sh and the Dockerfile's RUN steps are executed by Linux
#     shells (in CI and in the container). A CRLF-checked-out shell script fails with
#     the classic `\r: command not found` / `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r` no-such-file error.
#   - Solidity artifacts and the bytecode compiled from contracts/ are hashed, so a
#     line-ending change to a .sol file silently changes compiler output.
#   - evidence/benchmark.json is committed and diffed by hand; a wholesale CRLF
#     rewrite would bury real changes in noise.
#
# `text=auto` is deliberately not used: it lets Git guess per file. The explicit
# `eol=lf` below applies the same rule to everything, so there is nothing to guess.
* text eol=lf

# Binary files: never normalize, never diff as text. The repo tracks no binary assets
# today, so these are declared up front for the ones a project like this acquires --
# docs images, fonts, compiled native addons and wasm. Listing them now means the first
# such file added cannot be corrupted by normalization on the way in.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.wasm  binary
*.node  binary
*.gz    binary
*.zip   binary
*.sqlite binary

# SVG is text (it is XML) and should normalize like any other source file, but diffing
# it line by line is rarely useful. Keep it normalized, mark it non-diffable.
*.svg   text eol=lf -diff

# Generated and hand-maintained lockfile. Normalized like everything else, but excluded
# from diffs so a dependency bump does not swamp review with thousands of lines.
package-lock.json text eol=lf -diff linguist-generated
